Changes in v6:
- drop the eight hypercall counters this series was adding, along with
  struct ibmveth_hcall_stats and the adapter field holding it. Only
  reg_lan and free_lan had writers at this commit and none of the eight
  had a reader, and the ethtool -S keys v5 gave them in patch 11 are
  gone with them. This patch no longer touches ibmveth.h at all
- trace the logical-LAN registration, and the free retry in that same
  path, with netdev_dbg() instead. They fire on open/close and resize,
  not per packet, so a debug line is the right shape where a permanent
  counter was not. The queue teardown paths are left alone: they
  already report failures with netdev_err()
- document ibmveth_free_all_queues()'s log-and-continue contract in its
  kdoc, including that queue_handle[] is cleared whatever the hypercall
  returned
- clarified: the body now states that queue 0's handle is stored only
  on an H_SUCCESS registration
- clarified: the body drops the open-fail label walk rather than
  correcting it. Only the netif_set_real_num_rx_queues() failure enters
  out_unregister_queues
- clarified: the body drops the claim that ordering free_all_queues()
  before free_buffer_pools() stops PHYP retaining a registered LAN while
  its pools are released. It only held on H_SUCCESS
- commit message: restore three things the mailed v5 body carried and
  the rewrite dropped: the mixed register/free lifecycle that motivates
  extracting these helpers at all, the PAPR/PHYP full-teardown contract
  that makes one H_FREE_LOGICAL_LAN enough, and the note that runtime
  is still single-queue here so the with_handle arm cannot yet run

Changes in v5:
- Rename helpers to ibmveth_register_logical_lan() and
  ibmveth_free_all_queues()
- Retain single-queue registration for legacy paths

Changes in v4:
- Introduce register/free helpers in the same patch that wires their
  first open/close callers; keep subordinate-only helpers deferred
  until MQ enablement.
- Correct open/close unwind so free_all_queues() precedes
  free_buffer_pools().
- Drop the orphaned big-bang "open/close pipeline" patch from v3; that
  wiring is incremental across helper patches 3-7 instead.
